25
00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:48.060
And you, Obedience, give me back my sweet Jesus, don't cut me to the quick anymore.

26
00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:53.700
I pray you not to take the sight of my highest good away from me anymore.

27
00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:58.460
And I promise that even stammering I will write as you want."

28
00:01:58.460 --> 00:02:05.100
I only ask you, of you, the good grace to let me recover for a few days because my mind

29
00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:13.660
too little can no longer take being immersed in that vast ocean of divine charity, especially

30
00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:19.740
because in it I see my miseries and my ugliness more, and in seeing the love that God has

31
00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:22.900
for me, I feel I am almost going mad."

32
00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:31.020
Now, you see, this thing is being repeated again and that is the more you perceive God's

33
00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:34.660
love for you, the more you fall in love with him.

34
00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:37.140
That's what she calls "I'm going mad."

35
00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:42.620
But at the same time, you see all your own faults and miseries and failings as well.

36
00:02:42.620 --> 00:02:46.260
Because when you're looking at God you're looking at truth, and therefore you see the

37
00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:52.660
truth of yourself as well as the truth of everything else.

38
00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:58.620
So my mind too little can no longer take being immersed in that vast ocean of divine charity,

39
00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:03.860
especially because in it I can see my miseries and my ugliness more, and in seeing the love

40
00:03:03.860 --> 00:03:08.060
of God has for me, I feel I'm almost going mad.

41
00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:14.020
And so my weak nature feels faint and can take no more.

42
00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:16.220
Song of songs 2, 5.

43
00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:22.480
But in the meantime, I will occupy myself with writing about other things and then continue

44
00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:25.020
